1
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:03,840
If things between
Mr. Vijarn and me go any further…

2
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:05,400
Are you actually accepting his love?

3
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,080
Mr. Vijarn is just a second-class lawyer,

4
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:09,759
but his legal career

5
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:12,720
helped him build connections,
which led him into business.

6
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,000
An illegal business.

7
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:16,800
If you want to play a big game,
you must be bold.

8
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:19,200
Everything will go flawlessly.

9
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,320
I trust you completely.

10
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:23,120
No matter what,
don't agree to get engaged.

11
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,600
I care too much about you.

12
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:27,840
<i>He claims he cares,</i>
<i>but he never makes a move.</i>

13
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:30,240
After all, we aren't even related anymore.

14
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,960
In that case, I'm getting engaged.

15
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:33,040
Rajit, don't do this.

16
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,760
This has to be a grand event.

17
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:37,480
Every influential figure in Phuket
will be at our celebration.

18
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,720
Then, whatever you think is best.

19
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:52,800
Congratulations, Mr. Vijarn.

20
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:56,000
You're finally getting
the engagement you wanted.

21
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:02,040
That's because Rajit finally realized
how pathetic Thatri is.

22
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:05,000
Once he failed,
she immediately clung to me.

23
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,840
Your counter-strategy was perfect.

24
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,360
You predicted he'd bring the police
to raid the warehouse.

25
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:15,080
Not only did Thatri come up empty-handed,

26
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,880
you also secured the engagement.

27
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,000
Talk about killing
two birds with one stone.

28
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,640
Thatri is the only fool here.

29
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:29,200
After this, Thatri won't dare
call the police on us again.

30
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:32,880
This makes it a lot easier for us
to bring the drugs in.

31
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:37,320
So, have you figured out
how we're going to move the goods in?

32
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,160
Hey! Keep moving!

33
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:47,960
It's just like you said.

34
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,680
Thatri really sent him to spy on us.

35
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:54,480
If I knew you were this evil,

36
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,720
I would've thrown you in jail
back at the house.

37
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:05,080
How could you possibly know, you fool?

38
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:08,160
You're just a stupid, pathetic servant.

39
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,760
Should I take him out now?

40
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,519
This bastard really crossed me before.

41
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,880
Not yet. He might still be useful to us.

42
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,720
Keep him alive.

43
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:33,320
I had no idea Thatri was in Phuket.

44
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,320
If I'd known sooner,
I would've gotten rid of him for you.

45
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,720
I underestimated him.

46
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:42,360
I thought he ran back to Bangkok for good.

47
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,520
Who knew he'd return?

48
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:47,600
So you changed the plan.

49
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,320
Now, can you tell me

50
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,640
how you're going to smuggle the drugs in?

51
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,200
You asked

52
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:11,000
how I'd bring the drugs into Phuket?

53
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:13,160
There it is.

54
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:17,200
It comes by boat, docks at this pier,

55
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:21,200
gets loaded onto a truck,
and goes straight down this route.

56
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,280
Are you out of your mind?

57
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:27,280
Moving it out in the open like that?
If we hit a checkpoint, it's game over.

58
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,200
On my engagement day,

59
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,280
all the police in Phuket

60
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:34,040
will be here to provide security
for the influential figures.

61
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,200
Who on earth would be left

62
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,800
to set up a checkpoint?

63
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:43,080
No wonder you've been rushing
this engagement.

64
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,880
Honestly, this plan
isn't even that complex.

65
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:49,640
Thatri could easily figure it out.

66
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:51,680
That's why I tricked him
with the coffee beans,

67
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,920
to destroy his credibility.

68
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,600
If that day

69
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,080
he tries to call for police backup,

70
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:05,280
they won't believe a single word.

71
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,600
Please trust me just one more time.

72
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,280
Something is happening
on the engagement day.

73
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:25,800
If we don't act right now,
we're just letting them get away with it.

74
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:28,040
And what if there's nothing?

75
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:30,720
There is. I'm certain of it.

76
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:32,200
Evidence?

77
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:40,000
We don't know if Mr. Vijarn

78
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,840
will break the law again,

79
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:45,400
nor do we know if he'll do it today.

80
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,920
It's all just your speculation.

81
00:06:49,440 --> 00:06:51,680
When we found nothing
during the last raid,

82
00:06:51,760 --> 00:06:53,520
the governor reprimanded me.

83
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:55,560
If we come up
empty-handed again this time,

84
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:58,120
my career is officially over.

85
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,040
DOCTOR SOMSAK

86
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,360
You haven't checked on me in ages,

87
00:07:15,360 --> 00:07:18,760
but the moment
you're in trouble, you show up.

88
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,120
Look at yourself.

89
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,240
What am I supposed to do, Doc?

90
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:28,200
The police searched the place
and found nothing.

91
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:30,600
You got chewed out
and ruined your reputation.

92
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,240
Aren't you used to it by now?

93
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,760
It's not just about that, damn it, Doc.

94
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,160
Since we found nothing,

95
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,520
I'm out of options.

96
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:49,080
I'll have to watch Rajit
get engaged to that bastard.

97
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:53,880
If you don't want her to get engaged,
then steal her back.

98
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,280
Doc.

99
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,360
How can I do that?

100
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,600
Even if I take her away, what then?

101
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,880
I have nothing left.

102
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,680
I can barely take care of myself.

103
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:12,280
Then don't.

104
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,800
Just let her get engaged to someone else.

105
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:17,800
No! I can't accept that!

106
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,640
Then what do you want to do?

107
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,920
The reason I became a drunkard doctor

108
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:35,200
is because I suffered from heartbreak too.

109
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,840
I let her go,

110
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:42,360
and in the end,
I was left to suffer alone.

111
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,440
She went off and got married,

112
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,640
but she was never happy.

113
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:51,840
All I could do
was watch her from a distance,

114
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,680
completely helpless.

115
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:58,560
So, if you love her that much,

116
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,760
never let her go.

117
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,120
Do you understand?

118
00:09:10,480 --> 00:09:14,120
Wow. I poured my heart out.

119
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,320
DOCTOR SOMSAK

120
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,960
You just dozed off.

121
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,440
Doc.

122
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,920
Doc.

123
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,000
Why are you sleeping on the floor?

124
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:05,120
You kicked me out of bed
while you were asleep.

125
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,120
Still have the nerve to ask?

126
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,920
Get up since you're sober.
Sleeping on the floor is ruining my back.

127
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:14,920
-Go.
-I'm sorry.

128
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,800
That woman…

129
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:30,520
You love her a lot, don't you?

130
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,520
What did you say?

131
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,120
It's fine if you're still spacey.

132
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:46,480
Just go give it your all,

133
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:48,920
so you won't have to regret it later.

134
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:29,320
Miss Rajit is here.

135
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:41,320
<i>This bird is born with one wing and leg.</i>

136
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:42,600
Once it finds its partner,

137
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:45,640
<i>the two Biyi birds unite</i>
<i>to finally take flight,</i>

138
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,800
<i>staying together through thick and thin.</i>

139
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:52,160
<i>When one dies,</i>
<i>the other dies of a broken heart.</i>

140
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:55,680
<i>The Biyi bird represents</i>
<i>an unyielding love,</i>

141
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,720
<i>one that remains unchanged forever.</i>

142
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:01,240
Just go give it your all,

143
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,200
so you won't have to regret it later.

144
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:09,440
Oh, Tri. Why are you still sitting here?

145
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:12,880
I assumed you had already left
with Sasi to set up the venue.

146
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:17,360
If we went together, I'm afraid
you wouldn't be able to handle it,

147
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:20,440
seeing two ex-fiancés arrive
at an event together.

148
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:22,680
Fair point.

149
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:25,440
But it would be much better
if you stayed somewhere else,

150
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:29,080
rather than the house
of your ex-fiancée's husband.

151
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,800
I appreciate your honesty.

152
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,720
So let me be frank too.

153
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,160
I'm staying right here

154
00:13:36,880 --> 00:13:38,680
to prove my innocence.

155
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,720
Shall we head out?

156
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:46,560
Of course, dear.

157
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,880
As the representative
for the groom's side,

158
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:26,720
I formally ask
for Rajit's hand in engagement,

159
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:31,000
along with the dowry as agreed upon.

160
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,640
Please feel free to count it.

161
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:36,080
Everything is in order.

162
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:37,520
Thank you very much.

163
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:41,120
We don't care much for formalities,

164
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,160
so let's proceed to the next step.

165
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,360
I invite the bride to bow to the groom.

166
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,920
I don't approve of this engagement.

167
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,480
You have no say in this matter.

168
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:46,800
You have nothing to do with Rajit anymore.

169
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,120
Please leave.

170
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:52,120
I'm not leaving. I came here for Rajit,

171
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:54,440
and I'm not going anywhere.

172
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,560
Tri, what are you doing?

173
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:09,160
That is exactly how a brainless fool acts.
He was stupid in the past,

174
00:16:09,240 --> 00:16:11,160
and he is just as stupid now.

175
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:12,560
Mother.

176
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:21,560
Someone please escort Thatri out of here.

177
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,040
You just brought up rights.

178
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:27,240
So what right do you have to kick me out?

179
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,760
Is this your house or Rajit's?

180
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:39,600
Even if he's an imposter,
he's breathtakingly handsome.

181
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,800
Uncle Ree…

182
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:47,560
Crashing an engagement ceremony
like this, how fierce.

183
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,960
What do I have to do

184
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:55,800
to get a man to say that to me?

185
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,720
I'd run away with him in a heartbeat.

186
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,760
She has already agreed to marry me.

187
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:07,880
I suggest you leave.
Don't force her to reject you herself.

188
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,520
You'll only embarrass yourself.

189
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:12,920
I'm not going anywhere.

190
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:17,880
Mr. Thatri, I think you should stop.

191
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,040
Stop acting like such a sore loser.

192
00:17:25,240 --> 00:17:26,280
Rajit.

193
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:31,680
I love you, Rajit.

194
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,680
Mr. Thatri,

195
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:49,800
you aren't trying to ruin this engagement

196
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,120
because you're jealous of her, right?

197
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:53,920
Jealous? Of course not.

198
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:55,480
There's no such thing.

199
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:57,360
If that's true,

200
00:17:57,440 --> 00:18:00,640
do you even know
how they're moving the goods into Phuket?

201
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,880
Yes. Since the war ended,

202
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:06,000
only one road into Phuket remains usable.

203
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:07,480
Intercepting them will be easy.

204
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,240
Even so,

205
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:12,240
if I slip away to lead the police,

206
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,520
Mr. Vijarn will notice my absence,

207
00:18:15,600 --> 00:18:16,920
and our plan will be ruined.

208
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,240
What if I create a diversion

209
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:20,880
to draw everyone's attention,

210
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,000
allowing you to slip away?

211
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:27,840
This is way too insulting.

212
00:18:29,240 --> 00:18:31,360
-Too slow.
-What?

213
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:35,520
If you truly loved Rajit,
you would have punched me by now,

214
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:37,360
not stood there for a minute.

215
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:44,920
Now everyone sees
how differently we feel about you.

216
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:49,000
As for my feelings,
I've just confessed mine.

217
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,480
Right in front of all of you.

218
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:56,720
Miss Rajit, don't believe him.
He is tricking you,

219
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,480
just like he did countless times before.

220
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,560
A man like him is never sincere.

221
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:05,360
Rajit,

222
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,280
you are the only one

223
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:11,040
I will ever love.

224
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:17,400
Miss Rajit.

225
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:03,960
Come with me.

226
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:06,480
Yes.

227
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,280
Move.

228
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:35,440
Be careful.

229
00:20:38,840 --> 00:20:40,000
You came fully prepared.

230
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,320
Of course I did. It's all because of you.

231
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,200
Get in, quick.

232
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:56,880
You look beautiful today.

233
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,840
Uncle Ree! Let's go.

234
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,600
Quick.

235
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:10,480
Stop right there.

236
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:22,760
What? Hiding here?

237
00:21:28,480 --> 00:21:30,320
You're bringing me nothing but trouble.

238
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:33,960
I shouldn't have told you to fight back.
If you wanted to elope,

239
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:37,000
couldn't you two have done it on your own?

240
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:38,680
Why drag me into this mess?

241
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:41,240
We aren't eloping.

242
00:21:41,320 --> 00:21:44,520
We're just escaping the engagement.
Besides, we're doing this

243
00:21:44,600 --> 00:21:46,280
to catch Mr. Vijarn.

244
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,280
In that case, I'm getting engaged.

245
00:21:48,360 --> 00:21:50,720
Rajit, don't do this. I won't allow it.

246
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,800
Have you lost your mind?
Why would you do that?

247
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,040
Uncle Ree,

248
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,120
I'm risking myself

249
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:58,680
because I want to catch Mr. Vijarn.

250
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,360
The ceremony must happen,

251
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:05,000
so he feels safe enough
to smuggle the contraband.

252
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:07,000
That's when we strike

253
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:10,080
and ambush him red-handed.

254
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:14,440
But it will ruin your reputation.

255
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:20,040
It won't be ruined. I have a plan.

256
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,840
So this was your plan?

257
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:31,960
Still, it's better than letting you
get engaged to someone like him.

258
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:40,320
But why did you have to hide here?

259
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,120
Don't ask questions now.
Please look after her

260
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:44,720
and keep her out of sight.

261
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:48,480
There you go, ordering me around again.

262
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:49,760
Wait.

263
00:22:50,360 --> 00:22:52,560
Why are you leaving me here?

264
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,120
Where are you going, Uncle Ree?

265
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:56,040
I'm going to help the Chief.

266
00:22:56,120 --> 00:22:58,840
I can't let him fight this battle alone.

267
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:01,200
Wait. Hold on.

268
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,560
Before you go, tell me

269
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,200
how I am involved in this.

270
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:11,360
In all of Phuket,
I'm closest to the District Chief and you.

271
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:13,280
Who else would I ask for help?

272
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:14,880
Why even ask?

273
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:19,280
Great, calling me stupid now.

274
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:20,560
I'm off.

275
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,000
I'm leaving now.

276
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:23,440
Wait, Uncle Ree.

277
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:29,080
I wanted you to stop the ceremony, not to…

278
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,320
kiss me.

279
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:36,680
You opportunist.

280
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:46,320
DOCTOR SOMSAK

281
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:50,600
Please be careful.

282
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:28,760
Vijarn, did you find Rajit?

283
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,760
If I found her, she would be here with me.
Why even ask?

284
00:24:32,840 --> 00:24:35,360
Hey. Why speak to me like that?

285
00:24:35,440 --> 00:24:38,440
I asked nicely.
There's no need to snap at me.

286
00:24:40,320 --> 00:24:41,880
There's no need to chase her.

287
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:44,760
It looks like she ran away willingly.

288
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,480
Right?

289
00:24:47,040 --> 00:24:50,600
Or maybe she never wanted to get engaged,
but couldn't say no.

290
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:59,680
Mother, what are you laughing at?

291
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:01,120
It seems

292
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:04,320
Rajit and Thatri planned this
from the very beginning

293
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:07,120
to escape the ceremony.

294
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:10,360
Mother.

295
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:21,640
Hey, today is so easy.
It feels like a joyride.

296
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,240
Perks of having a smart boss.

297
00:25:25,320 --> 00:25:28,800
Drawing the police to the wedding
makes this smuggling too easy.

298
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:41,200
Hey. It's the police.

299
00:25:41,280 --> 00:25:42,280
What do we do?

300
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:44,760
Stay calm. It might be nothing.

301
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,640
Officer, is something wrong?

302
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:00,920
Sorry.

303
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:04,600
We received a tip
about illegal cargo being transported.

304
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,920
Let us search the vehicle.

305
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:22,320
Don't even think about it.

306
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,520
If you run, I will shoot.

307
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:25,440
Get out of the car.

308
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,360
Now!

309
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:30,240
Get out.

310
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:36,280
Turn around.

311
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:38,120
Turn around.

312
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:42,880
-Search it.
-Yes, sir.

313
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:49,080
Anyone got a knife?

314
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:08,800
We found coffee beans
and this package inside.

315
00:27:18,760 --> 00:27:19,920
Hand me the knife.

316
00:27:43,880 --> 00:27:45,720
Get in the car and move! Now!

317
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:47,640
-Yes, Boss.
-Let's go.

318
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,760
Damn it!

319
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:05,760
Go.

320
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:18,520
Damn it!

321
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:37,080
What is this?

322
00:28:37,160 --> 00:28:38,440
I have no idea either.

323
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:47,360
If you had actually helped me
during the ceremony,

324
00:28:47,440 --> 00:28:49,680
or at least caught Thatri,
it wouldn't have been ruined.

325
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,520
Hey, don't shift the blame to me.

326
00:28:52,600 --> 00:28:54,120
You couldn't even catch him,

327
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:56,520
that's why the whole thing fell apart.

328
00:28:56,600 --> 00:28:59,240
Hey, I even supported

329
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,200
your engagement to Rajit,

330
00:29:01,280 --> 00:29:03,760
so someone could manage the estate.

331
00:29:03,840 --> 00:29:06,040
And you throw a tantrum when it fails?

332
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:09,480
Good thing Thatri took her away.

333
00:29:09,560 --> 00:29:10,680
Say whatever you want.

334
00:29:10,760 --> 00:29:12,880
Go ahead and say it.
It's entirely up to you.

335
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:15,400
-Of course.
-But I'm not letting this slide.

336
00:29:15,480 --> 00:29:16,520
What?

337
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:26,040
Save that for later, Mr. Vijarn.

338
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:30,440
You need to prepare an excuse
for the police first.

339
00:29:43,200 --> 00:29:45,560
It looks just like a bag of flour.

340
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,960
Why did you bring this here?

341
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,720
It's not flour, Nid.

342
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:52,200
We don't know what it is yet,

343
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:54,000
but it's definitely illegal.

344
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,480
-What?
-Huh?

345
00:29:57,920 --> 00:29:59,880
If it's illegal,
why bring it into this house?

346
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:03,040
To get answers from its owner.

347
00:30:04,480 --> 00:30:05,600
Mr. Vijarn…

348
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:13,880
I suspect this engagement
was organized as a front

349
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:20,440
to distribute contraband
behind the scenes.

350
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:24,800
Am I right, Mr. Vijarn?

351
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:44,400
Governor, I truly know nothing about this.

352
00:30:46,040 --> 00:30:47,720
And what does this have to do with me?

353
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,520
Why accuse me like this?

354
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:55,800
You were caught red-handed,
and you still deny it?

355
00:30:57,680 --> 00:31:00,840
You don't even know
what this cargo is yet.

356
00:31:00,920 --> 00:31:04,560
Okay, if it's illegal as you claim,

357
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:07,560
it doesn't mean I'm involved.

358
00:31:08,160 --> 00:31:09,320
Am I right, District Chief?

359
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:15,680
Sir, what do you think?

360
00:31:17,040 --> 00:31:18,960
Could you come to the station?

361
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:22,840
To prove my innocence, I'd be glad to.

362
00:31:22,920 --> 00:31:24,200
No problem at all, sir.

363
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:26,960
But I hope,

364
00:31:27,040 --> 00:31:29,640
once you're done interrogating me,

365
00:31:29,720 --> 00:31:32,960
you question Thatri as well.

366
00:31:33,040 --> 00:31:34,880
He is highly suspicious.

367
00:31:34,960 --> 00:31:39,200
Doing nothing would be biased.

368
00:31:40,320 --> 00:31:42,040
Am I right, District Chief?

369
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:45,560
Sir, thank you for everything.

370
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:47,160
Until next time, sir.

371
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:48,200
Thank you.

372
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:04,440
DOCTOR SOMSAK

373
00:32:10,640 --> 00:32:11,800
Time to eat.

374
00:32:13,920 --> 00:32:16,320
You can eat first. I'm not hungry.

375
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:20,760
Great. I made all this food for nothing.

376
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:23,960
Good grief.

377
00:32:25,920 --> 00:32:27,160
Uncle Ree.

378
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:29,520
How did it go?

379
00:32:30,120 --> 00:32:32,040
Mr. Vijarn is currently
giving his statement,

380
00:32:32,120 --> 00:32:33,600
but he likely won't face charges.

381
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:35,560
He knows the law well,

382
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:38,640
and we lack eyewitnesses to convict him.

383
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:42,880
What a shame.

384
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:45,600
After everything we did,
we still couldn't catch him.

385
00:32:48,440 --> 00:32:50,680
You should stay here for a while.

386
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:54,080
Even though the ceremony is off,
Mr. Vijarn is still free.

387
00:32:54,160 --> 00:32:56,560
If you return to the house,
you'll be a sitting duck.

388
00:32:57,760 --> 00:32:58,880
I care about you.

389
00:33:07,840 --> 00:33:11,000
Here. I bought some clothes for you.

390
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,040
Thank you.

391
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:21,760
By the way, Uncle Ree,

392
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:25,120
how are things at Som Song Saeng House?

393
00:33:26,960 --> 00:33:28,160
I have no idea.

394
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:30,000
I didn't dare go inside,

395
00:33:30,080 --> 00:33:32,200
fearing they'd force me to bring you back.

396
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:36,000
You're quite the schemer, you know.

397
00:33:36,080 --> 00:33:39,120
Will anyone guess you planned this escape?

398
00:33:40,520 --> 00:33:42,440
I might have planned it,

399
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,560
but it wouldn't have succeeded

400
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:46,040
without your cooperation.

401
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:49,000
If this is wrong, we share the blame.

402
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:54,160
How could I not cooperate?

403
00:33:56,400 --> 00:33:58,640
I couldn't bear to watch you
marry another man.

404
00:34:25,520 --> 00:34:28,679
I love you, Rajit. You are the only one

405
00:34:28,760 --> 00:34:30,040
I will ever love.

406
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:57,120
That man…

407
00:34:58,480 --> 00:35:00,920
I couldn't bear to watch you
marry another man.

408
00:35:11,520 --> 00:35:14,680
I wanted you to stop the ceremony, not to…

409
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:17,400
kiss me.

410
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:19,960
You opportunist.

411
00:35:30,040 --> 00:35:30,920
What are you smiling at?

412
00:35:35,360 --> 00:35:37,840
Care to share
whatever is making you so happy?

413
00:35:40,360 --> 00:35:41,960
Is something wrong, District Chief?

414
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:45,920
I finally found out

415
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:47,840
what that seized cargo

416
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:49,240
actually is.

417
00:35:54,640 --> 00:35:55,600
What is it?

418
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:03,200
So this is heroin?

419
00:36:04,680 --> 00:36:06,800
I only heard about it
while studying in England.

420
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,000
This is my first time seeing it.

421
00:36:10,240 --> 00:36:11,360
Same here.

422
00:36:12,720 --> 00:36:14,600
It appeared over 40 years ago,

423
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:17,600
originally created for medical treatment.

424
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:20,920
But later on,
it became a narcotic. Heavy usage

425
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,640
destroys the user's brain,

426
00:36:22,720 --> 00:36:25,440
leaving them as neither human nor ghost.

427
00:36:26,240 --> 00:36:28,520
That is why its trade
is strictly prohibited.

428
00:36:31,840 --> 00:36:33,120
It's pure poison.

429
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:39,840
Smuggling contraband is bad enough,
but dealing drugs,

430
00:36:40,720 --> 00:36:41,760
it's utterly villainous.

431
00:36:43,120 --> 00:36:44,280
Worse yet,

432
00:36:45,960 --> 00:36:48,000
we can't convict Mr. Vijarn.

433
00:36:48,080 --> 00:36:49,600
We have the evidence,

434
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:51,360
but without witnesses,

435
00:36:51,440 --> 00:36:53,520
he can just claim it isn't his.

436
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:03,120
Then we must rely on Wai.

437
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:07,880
He's the only one
inside their inner circle.

438
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:09,760
He can testify

439
00:37:09,840 --> 00:37:12,240
or secure the evidence to convict him.

440
00:37:14,520 --> 00:37:15,400
Speaking of Wai,

441
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:18,000
we haven't heard from him in a while.

442
00:37:35,120 --> 00:37:36,320
Damn it.

443
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:39,680
The police managed to take our drugs away.

444
00:37:41,520 --> 00:37:43,360
Fortunately, they still
don't have evidence,

445
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:45,080
so they can't trace it back to us.

446
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:48,160
The key witness is right here.

447
00:37:56,680 --> 00:37:57,840
Hey, stop.

448
00:37:59,880 --> 00:38:00,960
Why stop?

449
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:03,160
Stomp him to death right now,

450
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:05,560
and then we can send
his body for Thatri to see.

451
00:38:06,080 --> 00:38:08,400
Doing this only gives us satisfaction.

452
00:38:08,480 --> 00:38:10,720
Wai is merely an underling.

453
00:38:11,320 --> 00:38:13,880
The person we need to kill is Thatri.

454
00:38:47,160 --> 00:38:49,600
You woke up so early. Where are you going?

455
00:38:49,680 --> 00:38:52,400
I'm going to the post office.

456
00:38:52,480 --> 00:38:53,800
The post office?

457
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:57,200
Why are you going there? Sasi is here,

458
00:38:57,920 --> 00:38:59,480
and you have no relatives in Bangkok.

459
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:02,120
I have my own errands to run.

460
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:06,040
You don't need to meddle
in my every piece of business.

461
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:26,520
Mister! Mister!

462
00:39:36,800 --> 00:39:38,960
Mister, your name is Thatri, right?

463
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,600
Yes. What is it, kid?

464
00:39:41,680 --> 00:39:43,200
Someone left this for you.

465
00:39:51,480 --> 00:39:53,480
I HAVE WAI. IF YOU WANT HIM ALIVE
YOU MUST COME FIND ME

466
00:40:05,240 --> 00:40:07,000
Their intention is to use Wai as a bait

467
00:40:07,080 --> 00:40:10,000
for you to go out so they can kill you.
You must not go.

468
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:12,520
I know, but if I don't go,

469
00:40:12,600 --> 00:40:13,880
Wai will die.

470
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:17,520
He was caught because he's my informant.

471
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:19,400
I have to go.

472
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,440
I will inform the police

473
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:24,360
and have them send backup for you.

474
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:25,520
No.

475
00:40:25,600 --> 00:40:27,600
The fact that they dared
to send this letter

476
00:40:27,680 --> 00:40:29,920
means they already anticipated the police.

477
00:40:31,040 --> 00:40:32,400
If they see any cops show up,

478
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:33,960
they will surely kill Wai.

479
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:42,760
Can you find a couple of guns for me?

480
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,280
I need them for self-defense.

481
00:40:48,800 --> 00:40:51,240
Follow me. I have something to show you.

482
00:41:35,640 --> 00:41:37,120
Are you going to destroy Phuket?

483
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:40,280
You're bringing trouble to me.

484
00:41:41,080 --> 00:41:43,200
These weapons belonged
to the Japanese army.

485
00:41:43,280 --> 00:41:46,360
When the war ended, they withdrew,

486
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:48,480
but left these behind.

487
00:41:48,560 --> 00:41:50,520
I already notified headquarters,

488
00:41:51,200 --> 00:41:54,160
but they have no budget for destruction,
so they must be kept here.

489
00:41:57,800 --> 00:42:00,880
So you are letting me
borrow these to fight them?

490
00:42:03,880 --> 00:42:06,720
They will be more useful
than the guns you asked for.

491
00:42:25,520 --> 00:42:26,680
Mr. Thatri.

492
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:31,600
If you don't care about yourself,

493
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:35,640
at least think of the person
you left behind.

494
00:42:52,920 --> 00:42:55,880
I risked everything to kidnap him
from Som Song Saeng House,

495
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:57,000
fearing you'd be lonely.

496
00:42:58,440 --> 00:42:59,640
I really was lonely.

497
00:43:00,240 --> 00:43:04,080
I missed you so much, Don Jose.

498
00:43:04,160 --> 00:43:05,920
DOCTOR SOMSAK

499
00:43:09,160 --> 00:43:10,280
Where is the doctor?

500
00:43:12,080 --> 00:43:14,160
He left for Phang Nga before dawn.

501
00:43:14,240 --> 00:43:17,640
They are short on doctors there,
so they asked him to help.

502
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:20,200
What a shame.

503
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:22,360
I was going to make delicious food for him

504
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:24,120
to say thanks for troubling him.

505
00:43:25,120 --> 00:43:25,960
Now I can't.

506
00:43:27,720 --> 00:43:29,840
You are going to cook, Uncle Ree?

507
00:43:30,760 --> 00:43:31,800
Yeah.

508
00:43:46,640 --> 00:43:49,520
Tell me if you need any help.

509
00:43:51,160 --> 00:43:52,520
I know you are a great cook.

510
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,000
But if it is Western food,

511
00:43:54,080 --> 00:43:56,320
an overseas student like me
won't lose to you.

512
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:00,920
-Oh no! The meat is burning!
-What!?

513
00:44:05,600 --> 00:44:06,680
You tricked me.

514
00:44:12,160 --> 00:44:13,040
Uncle Ree,

515
00:44:13,120 --> 00:44:16,120
why did you suddenly want to cook?

516
00:44:20,080 --> 00:44:21,200
It's nothing.

517
00:44:21,800 --> 00:44:24,200
I just wanted to show off my skills.

518
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:37,680
If you don't care about yourself,

519
00:44:38,280 --> 00:44:41,720
at least think of the person you
left behind.

520
00:44:49,200 --> 00:44:51,760
In that case,
I'll help prepare the vegetables.

521
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:54,360
I'm not afraid it will be inedible.

522
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:56,960
Just want to help so we can eat sooner.

523
00:44:58,320 --> 00:44:59,240
Suit yourself.

524
00:45:26,520 --> 00:45:28,680
DOCTOR SOMSAK

525
00:45:34,280 --> 00:45:35,440
Please, after you.

526
00:45:44,920 --> 00:45:46,480
Pardon me.

527
00:45:48,320 --> 00:45:50,000
Thank you.

528
00:45:57,080 --> 00:45:58,520
Shall we eat?

529
00:45:59,280 --> 00:46:00,360
Dig in darlin'.

530
00:46:00,440 --> 00:46:03,200
You will see just
how mighty fine my cookin' is.

531
00:46:03,280 --> 00:46:04,320
Hey?

532
00:46:05,120 --> 00:46:06,880
You can speak the Southern dialect too?

533
00:46:21,520 --> 00:46:22,480
How is it?

534
00:46:23,080 --> 00:46:24,280
This is mighty tasty.

535
00:46:25,680 --> 00:46:27,080
You're copying me.

536
00:46:46,520 --> 00:46:48,560
Is it that dangerous, Uncle Ree?

537
00:46:55,200 --> 00:46:56,160
What is?

538
00:46:57,320 --> 00:46:58,280
Well,

539
00:46:59,160 --> 00:47:01,040
what you're planning to do today.

540
00:47:17,560 --> 00:47:20,040
Suddenly, you brought Don Jose over

541
00:47:21,040 --> 00:47:22,640
and even cooked for me.

542
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:25,280
Don't you know?

543
00:47:25,360 --> 00:47:27,480
It's like

544
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:29,960
you want to make

545
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:34,800
every moment count.

546
00:47:37,200 --> 00:47:40,000
If it weren't dangerous,

547
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:42,360
you wouldn't be doing this.

548
00:47:54,040 --> 00:47:57,800
I would rather bleed
than see you shed a single tear.

549
00:48:00,840 --> 00:48:01,960
Please, don't cry.

550
00:48:14,320 --> 00:48:16,040
I will come back to you safely.

551
00:48:16,760 --> 00:48:18,280
I promise.

552
00:48:28,400 --> 00:48:30,120
Promise me, Uncle Ree.

553
00:48:32,720 --> 00:48:34,520
If you break this promise,

554
00:48:36,120 --> 00:48:38,800
I will never forgive you
for the rest of my life.

555
00:48:44,880 --> 00:48:46,320
It's not just you.

556
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:49,480
I wouldn't forgive myself either

557
00:48:50,160 --> 00:48:52,440
if I made you suffer.

558
00:50:06,960 --> 00:50:08,360
Eat up,

559
00:50:08,880 --> 00:50:10,640
before it becomes your last meal.

560
00:50:18,560 --> 00:50:20,480
Are you losing your mind out of fear?

561
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:22,720
If in the past

562
00:50:22,800 --> 00:50:25,440
Pirate Zhang Gong Cheng spoke like this,

563
00:50:25,520 --> 00:50:26,920
I would be scared.

564
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:30,480
But now,

565
00:50:30,560 --> 00:50:33,040
you are merely a servant
to a drug trafficker.

566
00:50:34,880 --> 00:50:36,840
A dog is more valuable than you.

567
00:50:41,080 --> 00:50:42,880
You have a big mouth.

568
00:50:42,960 --> 00:50:44,280
Are you from around here?

569
00:50:44,360 --> 00:50:45,760
What about it?

570
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,480
If you were local,

571
00:50:48,560 --> 00:50:51,400
you would have seen the opium dens
with your own eyes.

572
00:50:52,920 --> 00:50:55,840
You know how wretched opium addicts are.

573
00:50:55,920 --> 00:50:57,720
When craving opium,

574
00:50:57,800 --> 00:50:59,840
they sell their own children

575
00:51:00,440 --> 00:51:02,480
and wives…

576
00:51:05,120 --> 00:51:07,680
and even abuse their parents
just to smoke opium.

577
00:51:10,200 --> 00:51:11,840
And your devilish drug

578
00:51:11,920 --> 00:51:14,680
is thousands of times worse than opium.

579
00:51:15,280 --> 00:51:16,960
If you sell it,

580
00:51:17,040 --> 00:51:19,120
you are viler than an animal.

581
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:27,520
Struck a nerve, didn't I?
The great Pirate Zhang Gong Cheng,

582
00:51:27,600 --> 00:51:30,400
whose name used
to silence crying children,

583
00:51:30,480 --> 00:51:33,360
today you are so pathetic,
you must deal drugs.

584
00:51:39,120 --> 00:51:41,480
If you're trying to provoke me
into killing you,

585
00:51:41,560 --> 00:51:43,920
forget it.

586
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:46,800
You will stay alive until Thatri dies.

587
00:52:09,360 --> 00:52:11,520
Do you really think
Thatri would be stupid enough

588
00:52:11,600 --> 00:52:13,360
to throw his life away here,

589
00:52:13,440 --> 00:52:15,680
just to save a worthless trash like him?

590
00:52:15,760 --> 00:52:18,960
You are the trash. You wretched parasite.

591
00:52:20,480 --> 00:52:21,400
What did you say?

592
00:52:26,880 --> 00:52:28,200
Don't worry.

593
00:52:29,520 --> 00:52:33,240
I know him well. Thatri will show up.

594
00:52:35,000 --> 00:52:36,040
Good.

595
00:52:36,120 --> 00:52:39,520
Then we can settle
the score with interest.

596
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:47,080
He's here.

597
00:52:48,680 --> 00:52:50,320
Take cover first.

598
00:52:50,400 --> 00:52:52,080
Don't let him see your faces.

599
00:52:55,120 --> 00:52:55,960
Hey!

600
00:53:33,080 --> 00:53:34,160
Uncle Ree…

601
00:53:45,720 --> 00:53:47,320
Run! Mr. Thatri!

602
00:53:47,840 --> 00:53:49,200
Run!

603
00:53:57,720 --> 00:53:59,520
I kept my promise.

604
00:53:59,600 --> 00:54:02,600
If you have any honor left, release Wai.

605
00:54:02,680 --> 00:54:05,040
I admire your courage for coming,

606
00:54:05,120 --> 00:54:06,840
but I'm not the one who made a promise.

607
00:54:29,560 --> 00:54:30,960
Mr. Thatri!

608
00:54:47,520 --> 00:54:48,640
Hey.

609
00:54:48,720 --> 00:54:51,000
How was it this easy?

610
00:54:52,080 --> 00:54:53,600
Did Thatri really just walk out here

611
00:54:54,240 --> 00:54:56,000
like an idiot to get shot?

612
00:54:56,880 --> 00:54:59,680
I told you. He's loyal to his comrades.

613
00:55:00,200 --> 00:55:01,680
He was bound to show up.

614
00:55:01,760 --> 00:55:02,880
Sure.

615
00:55:03,680 --> 00:55:06,280
Hey, go get his body.

616
00:55:06,360 --> 00:55:08,280
I want to take a good look at his face.

617
00:55:24,680 --> 00:55:27,040
-Hey!
-Hey! Get down!

618
00:55:31,160 --> 00:55:32,000
I knew it.

619
00:55:33,840 --> 00:55:35,080
Wai, run!

620
00:55:42,440 --> 00:55:43,440
Wai!

621
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:49,360
He knows our secrets.
We can't let him escape alive.

622
00:55:49,440 --> 00:55:51,120
Cover me!

623
00:56:02,400 --> 00:56:05,280
I made a promise to you, Rajit,
that I would return.

624
00:56:05,360 --> 00:56:07,040
I refuse to die in this place.

625
00:56:12,320 --> 00:56:14,520
Surround him! Kill him!

626
00:56:15,280 --> 00:56:16,440
Go!

627
00:57:01,120 --> 00:57:02,560
Look out!

628
00:57:03,840 --> 00:57:05,160
He has bombs too?

629
00:57:05,240 --> 00:57:06,360
Hey! Where are you going?

630
00:57:06,440 --> 00:57:07,920
You coward.

631
00:57:09,800 --> 00:57:11,560
Are you brave enough to trade with me?

632
00:57:11,640 --> 00:57:12,840
As you wish.

633
00:57:14,560 --> 00:57:16,880
She comes to the post office so often,

634
00:57:17,880 --> 00:57:19,200
there must be a reason.

635
00:57:26,520 --> 00:57:29,840
Have you ever loved me at all?

636
00:57:31,280 --> 00:57:32,640
Please bring Miss Rajit back quickly.

637
00:57:32,720 --> 00:57:34,560
<i>Mr. Vijarn is going too far</i>

638
00:57:34,640 --> 00:57:37,000
<i>and taking over everything for her.</i>

639
00:58:03,400 --> 00:58:06,680
Subtitle translation by:
Khathathong Thongtumlueng
